- rule 6: warm light from the people's own lights: Warm patches on the set (walls, road): at 0.14 across, 0.77 down (3.1% of the frame; lit most by no-2-gateway-beam); at 0.47 across, 0.75 down (1.9% of the frame; lit most by no-2-gateway-beam); at 0.14 across, 0.86 down (0.7% of the frame; lit most by no-2-gateway-beam). Check each is lit by something you meant (a window, a lamp, the fire's glow on the road), not by a light meant for the notice that shines through or past it.

## Not checked by this tool

